            {
              "id": "glog-eba68afb-cf15-4e87-8b5b-bccac6446817",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Untrusted Data Deserialization Vulnerability in Pickle Modules\" is a security vulnerability in Python programming language that occurs when an application deserializes data from an untrusted source without proper validation. The `pickle` module in Python is used for serializing and deserializing objects, which can be exploited by an attacker to execute arbitrary code, if the data being deserialized is from an untrusted source.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the `pickle.loads()` function is used to deserialize data, which can be a potential security risk if the data is not trusted.\n\n```python\nstate = pickle.loads(state.detach().cpu().numpy().tobytes())\n```\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to avoid deserializing data from untrusted sources. If it is necessary to deserialize data, use a safe, standard data interchange format such as JSON or XML which do not allow arbitrary code execution.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nA safer alternative to the `pickle` module is the `json` module. Here is how you can use it:\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Assuming 'state' is a numpy array\nstate_list = state.detach().cpu().numpy().tolist()\nstate_json = json.dumps(state_list)\nstate = json.loads(state_json)\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `pickle` (built-in with Python)\n- `numpy`\n- `torch` (for the `detach()` and `cpu()` methods)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Python Security - Deserialization](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Deserialization_Cheat_Sheet.html#python)\n- [CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "B301"
                ]
              }
